text: ['(Start the game with this conspiracy face up in the command zone.)\\nAs long as every card in your card pool started the game in your library or in the command zone, lands you control have "{T}: Add one mana of any color."', '(Start the game with this conspiracy face up in the command zone.)\\nAt the beginning of the first upkeep, create a 1/1 colorless Construct artifact creature token with defender.', '(Start the game with this conspiracy face up in the command zone.)\\nDraw an additional hand of seven cards as the game begins. Before taking mulligans, shuffle all but one of your hands into your library.', '(Start the game with this conspiracy face up in the command zone.)\\nYou are the starting player. If multiple players would be the starting player, one of those players is chosen at random.', '(Start the game with this conspiracy face up in the command zone.)\\nYour minimum deck size is reduced by five.', 'Academy Elite enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the number of instant and sorcery cards in all graveyards.\\n{2}{U}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Academy Elite: Draw a card, then discard a card.', 'Add {R} for each tapped land your opponents control.', 'All damage that would be dealt this turn to target creature you control by a source of your choice is dealt to another target creature instead.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile X cards from your graveyard.\\nYou draw X cards and you lose X life.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nDraw two cards.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nSpontaneous Combustion deals 3 damage to each creature.', 'As long as Flaring Flame-Kin is enchanted, it gets +2/+2, has trample, and has "{R}: Flaring Flame-Kin gets +1/+0 until end of turn."', "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, Sulfuric Vortex deals 2 damage to that player.\\nIf a player would gain life, that player gains no life instead.", 'Attacking creatures get +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Brimstone Volley deals 3 damage to any target.\\nMorbid — Brimstone Volley deals 5 damage instead if a creature died this turn.', "Charging Rhino can't be blocked by more than one creature.", 'Choose two target creature cards in your graveyard. Sacrifice a creature. If you do, return the chosen cards to the battlefield tapped.', "Counter target activated or triggered ability. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)", 'Counter target spell. Its controller draws a card.\\nDraw a card.', "Cowards can't block Warriors.\\n{R}: Target creature becomes a Coward until end of turn.\\n{2}{R}: Target creature becomes a Warrior until end of turn.", 'Create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.\\nMorbid — Create three 2/2 green Wolf creature tokens instead if a creature died this turn.', 'Create a 4/4 red Ogre creature token. Starting with you, each player chooses an artifact, a creature, and a land from among the permanents controlled by the player to their left. Destroy each permanent chosen this way.', 'Creature tokens you control get +1/+1 and have vigilance.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever you tap a land for mana, add one mana of any type that land produced.', 'Creatures you control have haste.\\nSacrifice Fires of Yavimaya: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control with flying get +1/+1.', 'Creatures your opponents control get -2/-0 until end of turn.', 'Custodi Soulbinders enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the number of other creatures on the battlefield.\\n{2}{W}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Custodi Soulbinders: Create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', "Defender, flying\\n{1}{W}: Creatures you control with defender can attack this turn as though they didn't have defender.", 'Defender\\nWhen Cinder Wall blocks, destroy it at end of combat.', 'Defender\\nWhenever Pride Guardian blocks, you gain 3 life.', 'Defender\\nYour maximum hand size is increased by one.', 'Defender\\n{1}{R}, {T}: Vent Sentinel deals damage to target player or planeswalker equal to the number of creatures you control with defender.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment and up to one other target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment. Its controller gains 4 life.', "Destroy target artifact, target creature, target enchantment, and target land. (You can't cast this spell unless you have legal choices for all its targets.)", 'Destroy target creature or enchantment.', 'Destroy target creature with flying.', 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Destroy two target nonblack creatures. You lose 5 life.', 'Dethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)', 'Dethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nOther creatures you control have dethrone.\\nWhenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it dies, return that card to the battlefield under your control at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Dethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nPay 3 life: Add {R}.', "Dethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhenever Marchesa's Infiltrator deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.", "Dethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\n{1}{U}{R}: Target creature you control gains haste until end of turn and can't be blocked this turn.", "Draft Agent of Acquisitions face up.\\nInstead of drafting a card from a booster pack, you may draft each card in that booster pack, one at a time. If you do, turn Agent of Acquisitions face down and you can't draft cards for the rest of this draft round. (You may look at booster packs passed to you.)", 'Draft Canal Dredger face up.\\nEach player passes the last card from each booster pack to a player who drafted a card named Canal Dredger.\\n{T}: Put target card from your graveyard on the bottom of your library.', "Draft Cogwork Grinder face up.\\nAs you draft a card, you may remove it from the draft face down. (Those cards aren't in your card pool.)\\nCogwork Grinder enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the number of cards you removed from the draft with cards named Cogwork Grinder.", 'Draft Cogwork Librarian face up.\\nAs you draft a card, you may draft an additional card from that booster pack. If you do, put Cogwork Librarian into that booster pack.', 'Draft Deal Broker face up.\\nImmediately after the draft, you may reveal a card in your card pool. Each other player may offer you one card in their card pool in exchange. You may accept any one offer.\\n{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', 'Draft Whispergear Sneak face up.\\nDuring the draft, you may turn Whispergear Sneak face down. If you do, look at any unopened booster pack in the draft or any booster pack not being looked at by another player.', 'Drakestown Forgotten enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the number of creature cards in all graveyards.\\n{2}{B}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Drakestown Forgotten: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Draw four cards, then choose X cards in your hand and discard the rest.', 'Draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.', 'Each player loses 1 life for each creature they control.', 'Each player loses 1 life, discards a card, sacrifices a creature, then sacrifices a land.', 'Each player mills two cards. Then you put a creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.', 'Each player sacrifices a creature. Create an X/X black Demon creature token with flying, where X is the total power of the creatures sacrificed this way.', "Enchant creature\\nAs Traveler's Cloak enters the battlefield, choose a land type.\\nWhen Traveler's Cloak enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\nEnchanted creature has landwalk of the chosen type. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a land of that type.)", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.\\n{3}{U}: Attach Stasis Cell to target creature.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2, has vigilance, and can't attack you or planeswalkers you control.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+3.\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, create a 3/3 green Elephant creature token.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to any target."', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen Unquestioned Authority enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\nEnchanted creature has protection from creatures.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, return that card to the battlefield under your control.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals combat damage to a player, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Enchant creature\\n{R}: Enchanted creature gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Create a 1/1 green Squirrel creature token."', "Enchant land\\nEnchanted land is a 2/6 white Wall creature with defender. It's still a land.\\nWhen enchanted land dies, return that card to its owner's hand.", "Equipped creature gets +2/+2.\\nAs long as equipped creature has defender, it can attack as though it didn't have defender.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2.\\nWhenever equipped creature dies, you may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield and attach Deathrender to it.\\nEquip {2}', 'Equipped creature has double strike. (It deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Exile Ill-Gotten Gains. Each player discards their hand, then returns up to three cards from their graveyard to their hand.', 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', 'First strike\\nDethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)', 'First strike\\nSacrifice Vampire Hexmage: Remove all counters from target permanent.', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and attacks each combat if able.', "Flash\\nFlying\\nWhen Crookclaw Transmuter enters the battlefield, switch target creature's power and toughness until end of turn.", 'Flying, first strike', 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying\\nAs long as Pristine Angel is untapped, it has protection from artifacts and from all colors.\\nWhenever you cast a spell, you may untap Pristine Angel.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "Flying\\nDethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhenever Scourge of the Throne attacks for the first time each turn, if it's attacking the player with the most life or tied for most life, untap all attacking creatures. After this phase, there is an additional combat phase.", 'Flying\\nIslandcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for an Island card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', "Flying\\nPlayers can't cast spells during combat.\\n{R}: Target creature attacks this turn if able.", "Flying\\nWhen Liliana's Specter enters the battlefield, each opponent discards a card.", 'Flying\\nWhen Screaming Seahawk enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a card named Screaming Seahawk, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "Flying\\nWhenever Brago, King Eternal deals combat damage to a player, exile any number of target nonland permanents you control, then return those cards to the battlefield under their owner's control.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Jetting Glasskite becomes the target of a spell or ability for the first time each turn, counter that spell or ability.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature with flying dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Soulcatcher.', 'Flying\\nWill of the council — When Custodi Squire enters the battlefield, starting with you, each player votes for an artifact, creature, or enchantment card in your graveyard. Return each card with the most votes or tied for most votes to your hand.', 'Flying\\nWill of the council — When Magister of Worth enters the battlefield, starting with you, each player votes for grace or condemnation. If grace gets more votes, each player returns each creature card from their graveyard to the battlefield. If condemnation gets more votes or the vote is tied, destroy all creatures other than Magister of Worth.', 'Flying\\n{2}{U}: Tap target creature with flying.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', "Galvanic Juggernaut attacks each combat if able.\\nGalvanic Juggernaut doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nWhenever another creature dies, untap Galvanic Juggernaut.", "Grenzo, Dungeon Warden enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}: Put the bottom card of your library into your graveyard. If it's a creature card with power less than or equal to Grenzo's power, put it onto the battlefield.", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nDethrone (Whenever this creature attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nCreatures you control with the chosen name have "{T}: Add one mana of any color."', 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nCreatures you control with the chosen name have haste.', 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nEach creature you control with the chosen name enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nSpells with the chosen name you cast cost {1} less to cast.', 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nWhenever a creature with the chosen name enters the battlefield under your control, you may search your library for any number of cards with that name, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell with the chosen name, you may copy it. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell with the chosen name, you may draw a card.', 'Hidden agenda (Start the game with this conspiracy face down in the command zone and secretly choose a card name. You may turn this conspiracy face up any time and reveal that name.)\\nYou may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast spells with the chosen name.', "Ignition Team enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the number of tapped lands on the battlefield.\\n{2}{R}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Ignition Team: Target land becomes a 4/4 red Elemental creature until end of turn. It's still a land.", 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', 'Look at the top five cards of your library. You may reveal any number of creature cards from among them and put the revealed cards into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Morbid — At the beginning of each end step, if a creature died this turn, you may draw a card.', 'Morbid — When Morkrut Banshee enters the battlefield, if a creature died this turn, target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.', 'Morbid — When Wakedancer enters the battlefield, if a creature died this turn, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', "Multikicker {1}{B} (You may pay an additional {1}{B} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nSwampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\nQuag Vampires enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each time it was kicked.", 'Multikicker {1}{G} (You may pay an additional {1}{G} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nGnarlid Pack enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each time it was kicked.', 'Multikicker {1}{R} (You may pay an additional {1}{R} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nHaste\\nSkitter of Lizards enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each time it was kicked.', "Multikicker {1}{U} (You may pay an additional {1}{U} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nIslandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nEnclave Elite enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each time it was kicked.", 'Multikicker {1}{W} (You may pay an additional {1}{W} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nFlying\\nApex Hawks enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each time it was kicked.', 'Multikicker {G} (You may pay an additional {G} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nWhen Wolfbriar Elemental enters the battlefield, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token for each time it was kicked.', 'Multikicker {R} (You may pay an additional {R} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nWhen Deathforge Shaman enters the battlefield, it deals damage to target player or planeswalker equal to twice the number of times it was kicked.', 'No more than one creature can attack each combat.\\nNo more than one creature can block each combat.', 'Orcish Cannonade deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.\\nDraw a card.', 'Parley — Each player reveals the top card of their library. For each nonland card revealed this way, you create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying. Then each player draws a card.', 'Parley — Each player reveals the top card of their library. For each nonland card revealed this way, you create a 3/3 green Elephant creature token. Then each player draws a card.', "Parley — When Selvala's Enforcer enters the battlefield, each player reveals the top card of their library. For each nonland card revealed this way, put a +1/+1 counter on Selvala's Enforcer. Then each player draws a card.", 'Parley — {T}: Each player reveals the top card of their library. For each nonland card revealed this way, add {G} and you gain 1 life. Then each player draws a card.', 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn. You gain 1 life for each attacking creature.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nMorbid — Put three +1/+1 counters on that creature instead if a creature died this turn.', 'Reach', "Realm Seekers enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the total number of cards in all players' hands.\\n{2}{G}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Realm Seekers: Search your library for a land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", 'Regenerate each creature you control.', "Return target permanent you control and target permanent you don't control to their owners' hands.", 'Reveal Aether Searcher as you draft it. Reveal the next card you draft and note its name.\\nWhen Aether Searcher enters the battlefield, you may search your hand and/or library for a card with a name noted as you drafted cards named Aether Searcher. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. If you searched your library this way, shuffle.', 'Reveal Cogwork Spy as you draft it. You may look at the next card drafted from this booster pack.\\nFlying', 'Reveal Cogwork Tracker as you draft it and note the player who passed it to you.\\nCogwork Tracker attacks each combat if able.\\nCogwork Tracker attacks a player you noted for cards named Cogwork Tracker each combat if able.', "Reveal Lore Seeker as you draft it. After you draft Lore Seeker, you may add a booster pack to the draft. (Your next pick is from that booster pack. Pass it to the next player and it's drafted this draft round.)", "Reveal Lurking Automaton as you draft it and note how many cards you've drafted this draft round, including Lurking Automaton.\\nLurking Automaton enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the highest number you noted for cards named Lurking Automaton.", 'Reveal Paliano, the High City as you draft it. The player to your right chooses a color, you choose another color, then the player to your left chooses a third color.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color chosen as you drafted cards named Paliano, the High City.', 'Reveal the top five cards of your library. An opponent separates those cards into two piles. Put one pile into your hand and the other into your graveyard.', 'Sacrifice Sakura-Tribe Elder: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "Sacrifice a creature: Target player mills cards equal to the sacrificed creature's power.", 'Syphon Soul deals 2 damage to each other player. You gain life equal to the damage dealt this way.', 'Target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Target creature can block any number of creatures this turn.', 'Target creature gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nMorbid — That creature gets -13/-13 until end of turn instead if a creature died this turn.', 'Target player draws three cards. Then that player discards two cards unless they discard a land card.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nVolcanic Fallout deals 2 damage to each creature and each player.", 'Trample, haste\\nWhenever Barbed Shocker deals damage to a player, that player discards all the cards in their hand, then draws that many cards.', 'Trample\\nParley — Whenever Woodvine Elemental attacks, each player reveals the top card of their library. For each nonland card revealed this way, attacking creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn. Then each player draws a card.', 'Trample\\nWhen Pelakka Wurm enters the battlefield, you gain 7 life.\\nWhen Pelakka Wurm dies, draw a card.', "Untap target creature you don't control. That creature blocks this turn if able.\\nDraw a card.", 'Vigilance\\nPlainscycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Plains card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', "Vigilance\\nWhen Glimmerpoint Stag enters the battlefield, exile another target permanent. Return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'When Doomed Traveler dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'When Gamekeeper dies, you may exile it. If you do, reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a creature card. Put that card onto the battlefield and put all other cards revealed this way into your graveyard.', 'When Howling Wolf enters the battlefield, you may search your library for up to three cards named Howling Wolf, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Peace Strider enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', "When Phage the Untouchable enters the battlefield, if you didn't cast it from your hand, you lose the game.\\nWhenever Phage deals combat damage to a creature, destroy that creature. It can't be regenerated.\\nWhenever Phage deals combat damage to a player, that player loses the game.", 'When Pitchburn Devils dies, it deals 3 damage to any target.', 'When Runed Servitor dies, each player draws a card.', 'When Terastodon enters the battlefield, you may destroy up to three target noncreature permanents. For each permanent put into a graveyard this way, its controller creates a 3/3 green Elephant creature token.', 'Whenever Copperhorn Scout attacks, untap each other creature you control.', 'Whenever Hydra Omnivore deals combat damage to an opponent, it deals that much damage to each other opponent.', 'Whenever Infectious Horror attacks, each opponent loses 2 life.', 'Whenever Spiritmonger deals damage to a creature, put a +1/+1 counter on Spiritmonger.\\n{B}: Regenerate Spiritmonger.\\n{G}: Spiritmonger becomes the color of your choice until end of turn.', 'Whenever a creature deals combat damage to one of your opponents, its controller may draw a card.', "Whenever equipped creature attacks, look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card, you may put it onto the battlefield tapped.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", "Whenever players finish voting, each opponent who voted for a choice you didn't vote for loses 2 life.", 'While voting, you get an additional vote. (The votes can be for different choices or for the same choice.)', 'Will of the council — At the beginning of your upkeep, starting with you, each player votes for carnage or homage. If carnage gets more votes, sacrifice Coercive Portal and destroy all nonland permanents. If homage gets more votes or the vote is tied, draw a card.', 'Will of the council — Choose target instant or sorcery spell. Starting with you, each player votes for denial or duplication. If denial gets more votes, counter the spell. If duplication gets more votes or the vote is tied, copy the spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', "Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for a nonland permanent you don't control. Exile each permanent with the most votes or tied for most votes.", 'Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for death or torture. If death gets more votes, each opponent sacrifices a creature. If torture gets more votes or the vote is tied, each opponent loses 4 life.', 'Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for sickness or psychosis. If sickness gets more votes, creatures your opponents control get -2/-2 until end of turn. If psychosis gets more votes or the vote is tied, each opponent discards two cards.', 'Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for time or knowledge. If time gets more votes, take an extra turn after this one. If knowledge gets more votes or the vote is tied, draw three cards.', 'Will of the council — When Council Guardian enters the battlefield, starting with you, each player votes for blue, black, red, or green. Council Guardian gains protection from each color with the most votes or tied for most votes.', "Wrap in Flames deals 1 damage to each of up to three target creatures. Those creatures can't block this turn.", "You may cast Rout as though it had flash if you pay {2} more to cast it. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nDestroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'You may cast spells as though they had flash.', "You may exile a blue card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nChange the target of target spell with a single target.", "You may have Dack's Duplicate enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has haste and dethrone. (Whenever it attacks the player with the most life or tied for most life, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'You may play an additional land on each of your turns.', '[+1]: Target player draws two cards, then discards two cards.\\n[−2]: Gain control of target artifact.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "Whenever you cast a spell that targets one or more permanents, gain control of those permanents."', '{1}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Construct artifact creature token with defender.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature with defender: Flamewright deals 1 damage to any target.', '{1}{U}{B}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. Dimir Doppelganger becomes a copy of that card, except it has this ability.', '{1}{W}, Sacrifice Silverchase Fox: Exile target enchantment.', '{2}{R}: Target creature attacks this turn if able.', "{3}: Put target card from a graveyard on the bottom of its owner's library.", '{3}{U}, {T}: Look at the top X cards of your library, where X is the highest mana value among artifacts you control. You may put an artifact card from among them onto the battlefield. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', '{B}: Regenerate Twisted Abomination.\\nSwampcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Swamp card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{R}, Sacrifice Torch Fiend: Destroy target artifact.', '{R}: Chartooth Cougar gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nMountaincycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Mountain card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}, Sacrifice Magus of the Mirror: Exchange life totals with target opponent. Activate only during your upkeep.', '{T}: Add one mana of any type that a land you control could produce.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Quicksand: Target attacking creature without flying gets -1/-2 until end of turn.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Put a charge counter on Mirrodin's Core.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Mirrodin's Core: Add one mana of any color.", '{T}: Add {G}{G}{G}.\\nForestcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Forest card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Choose a creature card name. Reveal the top four cards of your library and put all of them with that name into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', '{T}: Choose a player. That player adds one mana of any color they choose.', "{T}: Heartless Hidetsugu deals damage to each player equal to half that player's life total, rounded down.", '{T}: Target land you control becomes the basic land type of your choice until end of turn.', '{T}: Target player draws a card, then discards a card.', '{X}, Sacrifice Pernicious Deed: Destroy each artifact, creature, and enchantment with mana value X or less.']
flavor: ['"Ajani goes where he is needed most and in his name we keep his lands safe."', '"All who set foot in Paliano are pawns in someone\'s play for power."\\n—Marchesa, the Black Rose', '"And Muzzio says my arguments have no teeth."\\n—Selvala, ranger of the Lowlands', '"Any good prospector must sift the gold from the sand."', '"Any hotheaded cub can raise a sword in anger."', '"As my father taught, \'Training will raise your shield to the blow, but courage fills the gaps the shield leaves open.\'"', '"Be careful in your hunt. The clever little creature can steal your wards and lead you right into the werewolf\'s den."\\n—Britta, midwife of Gatstaf', '"Behold! The image of the enemy and all that she has. Trust your envy, and take it."', '"Creation is a paradox. It hatches from its opposite."\\n—Olka, Mistmeadow witch', '"Crispy! Scarback! Load another volcano-ball."\\n—Stumphobbler Thuj, orcish captain', '"Die. But die knowing that your pathetic life will yield a great bounty for me."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Don\'t worry, your death will be as informative as possible."\\n—Gorghul, augur of skulls', '"End this. What I seek is far greater."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Everything comes with a price. Especially revolution."\\n—Grenzo, dungeon warden', '"Fear not. Your life will not go unlived."', '"Four parts molten bronze, yes . . . one part frozen mercury, yes, yes . . . but then what?"', '"Heat of battle" is usually a metaphor.', '"How can we outrun the sky?"\\n—Hadran, sunseeder of Naya', '"I am not at liberty to reveal my sources, but I can assure you, the price on your head is high."', '"I prefer loyalty to be a matter of respect, not of magic. But one does what one must."\\n—Kaalia of the Vast', '"If they board us we\'re finished," warned Orim. Crovax nodded. "And if they don\'t . . . what then?"', '"In the market for an alternative, friend?"', '"Is it wrong to go straight for what you want? Sneaking is for cats and goblins."\\n—Tahngarth of the *Weatherlight*', '"It is not that you will go mad. It is that you will beg for madness."\\n—Volrath', '"It\'s simple, really. If they can\'t find us, they can\'t kill us."', '"Just a moment of perfect grace and sanctity is enough."\\n—Kal Lior, leonin elder', '"Let go your grudges, or risk wandering the bogs forever in a murderous rage."\\n—Hildin, priest of Avacyn', '"Let nothing own the skies but the wind."\\n—Dejara, Giltwood druid', '"Let their mindless armies come and face the might of genius."\\n—Varil, Neurok partisan', '"Like a strain of music: easy to remember but impossible to catch."\\n—Mirri of the *Weatherlight*', '"Look at her, once filled with innocence. Death has a way of wringing away such . . . deficiencies."\\n—Savra', '"May starving fleas birth a thousand generations on your stubborn hide, cow!"\\n—Bruse Tarl, Goma Fada nomad', '"My faith is stronger than fang, claw, or mindless hunger."', '"My rule persists beyond death itself."', '"Never start a fight you can\'t finish."\\n—Padril, council guardian', '"Now everyone knows what you are."', '"Only when we journey into the unknown can we find the impossible."\\n—Cyrul the Wanderer', '"Our pyromancer\'s flames may not have killed them, but they bought us the time we needed."\\n—*The War Diaries*', '"Remember the fable of the elf who came upon a cave of gold. In trying to free the largest piece, she was crushed by its weight."\\n—Karn', '"Removing the encumbrance of useless brain tissue grants several advantages: a slight increase in mobility, a response of revulsion and horror from the enemy, and, in the case of large specimens, room for passengers."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Secrets, like coins, are easy to steal."', '"Superior force meets woefully inadequate object. What paradox were you expecting?"\\n—Azguri, archmage of Evos Isle', '"Take my hand and dance to the music of the winds."', '"The Black Rose doesn\'t tolerate weeds."', '"The Lowlands refuse to suffer at the whims of the High City."', '"The Vanished must have sent it from beyond to aid us in this struggle."\\n—Kessla, Sylvok shaman', '"The beneficent council deems you worthy of favor. They hope this doesn\'t provoke envy from your peers."', '"The end is justified in being mean. Or something like that."', '"The finest minions know what I need without me ever saying a thing."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"The smell of roasted flesh hung over the valley for hours."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"The timeless, tireless jaws of nature shall one day devour us all."\\n—Sildark, artificer of Omu', '"The wind smells of misfortune. Check your knots."\\n—Anitan, Ondu cleric', '"Their guards are soft, ready to welcome a sharp dagger."', '"Their spirits walk the winds and fill my soul."', '"They don\'t move much, but then again, if you get caught in its web, it has all the time in the world to get to you."\\n—Saidah, Joraga hunter', '"This is how wars are won—not with armies of soldiers but with a single knife blade, artfully placed."\\n—Yurin, royal assassin', '"Try to pretend like you understand what\'s important."', '"Unusual. Security also worth stealing."\\n—Dack Fayden', '"Watch your head . . . and your back."', '"We remember. We rise."', '"We should learn from the hydra. It never plays favorites; it devours everyone equally."\\n—Thrass, elder druid', '"Werewolves are an unholy mix of a predator\'s instinct and a human\'s hatred."\\n—Alena, trapper of Kessig', '"Why listen to the mumblings of wizards when the lash speaks true?"', '"Wind is forceful, yet ephemeral. It can knock a dragon out of the sky, yet pass through the smallest crack unhindered."\\n—Jestus Dreya, *Of Elements and Eternity*', '"Yawgmoth," Freyalise whispered as she set the bomb, "now you will pay for your treachery."', '"You have not died until I consent."', '"Your defiance is noted."', '"Zendikar fortifies itself against the Great Threat, making sentries of sky, sea, and stone."\\n—*The War Diaries*', 'A flame-kin is always formidable, but feeding its fire with a sorcerous gift grants it the power to devastate armies.', 'A single seed unleashes a flurry of growth.', 'After Gideon cleansed the Ninth District, none of the ganglords challenged the Boros.', 'Agreements with demons seldom end at the grave.', 'Anarchy comes in many forms: social, individual, Gruul . . .', "As Phage drank their energy, a vague memory of Jeska stirred. Then she lost herself again in the joy of her victims' suffering.", 'Devils redecorate every room with fire.', 'Does it reflect the future that once was or the past that can never be?', "Don't let its appearance frighten you. Let its claws and teeth do that.", 'Each volume contains wonders.', 'Fangren spur may sound louder, but Viridian resurgents claim that the horn of the vorrac creates a truer, more inspiring note.', 'Fervid shamans willingly submit to shockers in hopes of glimpsing the fortunes of the future.', "He vowed he would never rest until he reached his destination. He doesn't know how right he was.", 'Hers is an ancient form of necromancy, steeped in shamanic trance and ritual that few skaberen or ghoulcallers comprehend.', 'Hidetsugu held over a dozen oni in blood oath. At his touch, rocks scorched. At his word, cities burned.', 'His family was a small price to pay for the dark gifts that called to him.', "If you want to wreak havoc above, sometimes it's best to look below.", 'In Urborg, the instigators of each new rebellion are soaked in the blood of the last.', 'In life, they were a motley crew: farmers, lords, cutpurses, priests. In death, they are united in singular, benevolent purpose.', 'In the treetops, unseen by many, lurks chittering, skittering death.', 'It eats what it wants to eat—which is anything that moves.', 'Its pulsating cry shatters bonds of iron, granite, and servitude.', "Keldon warriors don't need signals to tell them when to attack. They need signals to tell them when to stop.", 'Kidnappers caught in Havengul are given two choices: languish in prison or become rat catchers. The smart ones go to prison.', 'Lanterns carved from the mystic stones of the Reito Mines were said to light the way of lost souls.', "Linger on death's door and risk being invited in.", "Long thought to be extinct, flocks of gryffs reappeared with Avacyn's return.", "Many who cross Sorin's path come down with a sudden and fatal case of being-in-the-way-of-a-millennia-old-vampire.", "Nature's strength outlives the strong.", 'Not all deaths are etched with mythic meaning and iconic glory.', 'Not once in the history of Grixis has anyone died of old age.', 'On Fiora, no matter is settled until King Brago offers an opinion.', "Paliano's creations provide ample opportunities to plot the downfall of a neighbor.", 'Sacred rites repurposed to fight an ancient threat.', 'Scholars had puzzled for centuries over the ruins at Tal Terig. Its secrets had always lived within one rune-carved head.', 'Scholars say that arbiters exist on every world, created by an unknown hand to enforce justice.', "Selvala's arrival never goes unnoticed.", 'Slain warriors were buried with a tree sapling, so they would become a part of the forest after death.', 'Some nature mages unknowingly took advantage of the temporal energies still swirling on Dominaria. What they mistook for healing magic was in fact the manipulation of time.', 'Spy for today. Plan for tomorrow.', 'Take away a few things, and a rebellion may ensue. Take away everything, and the oppression will be accepted as fate.', "The Neurok buried entangling cables just under the Quicksilver Sea. One seastrider harvest can provide an army's worth of armor and shields.", 'The Orzhov started using hawks as messengers in order to bypass the many toll roads and bridges that dot Ravnica. Soon the service became one of their most profitable businesses.', 'The Quicksilver Sea hissed and bubbled at the indignity. The Vulshok shaman just smiled.', 'The Simic created the cells to preserve their experiments. The Azorius put the cells to use on the guilty.', 'The best defense is a good offense.', 'The bolt struck with a flash, and there was a terrible sound, as of glass shattering, but the creature was unharmed.', 'The cinders believe their flame was stolen by one they call the Extinguisher. All who now wield fire draw their desperate wrath.', 'The first searchlights were given as gifts, symbols of cooperation, to the emissaries present at the signing of the Guildpact.', "The ideas came flooding in so fast that they couldn't all be contained.", 'The ingenuity of goblins, the depravity of demons, and the smarts of sheep.', 'The land drank power from the Mirari as though it had thirsted forever.', 'The mizzium-sphere array drove her mind deep into the thought field, where only the rarest motes of genius may be plucked.', 'The model incorporated the fifth sun effortlessly, as if it had always known.', 'The scrollkeepers never stepped an inch away from the doors of the Great Library, not even when the ogres and their oni masters swept through Minamo.', 'The smallest seed of regret can bloom into redemption.', 'The wurms become so big, a single scale can be used as a roof for a human dwelling.', 'Their language may be a cacophonous agglomeration of chittering snorts and mad barking, but the message they send is all too clear.', 'There are many ruins, but there used to be many more.', "Those who can't conspire, create.", 'Urza thought it a crusade. Xantcha knew it was a robbery.', 'When every right is voted away, only rage remains.', 'When its power is threatened, the council speaks with a unified voice.', 'When the blood hunt lost its thrill, she looked for less tangible means of domination.', 'Why wait for answers?', 'Yavimaya lights the quickest path to battle.']
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Allen Williams', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Austin Hsu', 'Bob Petillo', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Brian Hagan', 'Brom', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chase Stone', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dallas Williams', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Daren Bader', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'Donato Giancola', 'Drew Baker', 'E. M. Gist', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eric Fortune', 'Esad Ribic', 'Evan Shipard', 'Eytan Zana', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'James Paick', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jasper Sandner', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeff Simpson', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'John Donahue', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Stanko', 'Julie Dillon', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Karla Ortiz', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Mark A. Nelson', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Michael Komarck', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Sass', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Robbie Trevino', 'Roger Raupp', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Scott Hampton', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Shelly Wan', 'Shishizaru', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Véronique Meignaud', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Zoltan Boros', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai']
